<h1 style="margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: #0f172a;">
  You already have an account
</h1>

<p style="margin: 0 0 24px; font-size: 15px; color: #64748b; line-height: 1.6;">
  Someone just tried to sign up for Messy with <%= @user.email %>, and that address already has a login. No new account was created and nothing about your account has changed.
</p>

<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin: 0 0 28px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="border-radius: 9999px; background: #3b82f6;">
      <a href="<%= @login_link %>" style="display: inline-block; padding: 12px 28px; font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 9999px;">
        Sign in to Messy
      </a>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5;">
  If that was you, just sign in above. If it wasn't, you can ignore this email — signing in always requires a link sent to this address, so nobody else can get in.
</p>
